            <div xml:id="d397">

                <pb facs="0407" n="395" sameAs="frus:frus1941v01/pg395"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00111A Ports/54a</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to Diplomatic Officers in the
                        American Republics </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1941-11-07">November 7,
                        1941</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sirs</hi>: The Department of State has been informed
                    by the British Embassy that a considerable number of British merchant vessels
                    are being equipped with fighter aircraft to be used solely for defensive
                    purposes. The Embassy stated:</p>
                <p>[Here follows text of paragraph 3 (with the omission of the first two sentences),
                    paragraph 4, and paragraph 5 of the British <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >aide-mémoire</hi> of April 7, 1941, printed on <ref target="#pg387">page
                        387</ref>.]</p>
                <p>The Department of State replied to the British Embassy on July 24, 1941, as
                    follows:</p>
                <p>[Here follows the text of the second paragraph of <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >aide-mémoire</hi> to the British Embassy, dated July 24, 1941, printed on
                        <ref target="#pg392">page 392</ref>.]</p>
                <p>You are requested to bring the foregoing to the attention of the government to
                    which you are accredited.</p>
                <p>Very truly yours,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Cordell Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
